  'verde-river-sheep-parsons': 'The Friends of the Verde River map locates Sheep Crossing at 34.6740,-111.9412 and marks it as a difficult, long boat haul, but does not identify the water-entry edge. Keep withheld until the river landing is located and the access carry is mapped. See docs/access-remediation/2026-09-17-batch-30/review.json.',
  'verde-river-skidmore-sheep-crossing': 'The Friends of the Verde River map locates Sheep Crossing at 34.6740,-111.9412 and marks it as a difficult, long boat haul, but does not identify the water-entry edge. Keep withheld until the river landing is located and the access carry is mapped. See docs/access-remediation/2026-09-17-batch-30/review.json.',
  'verde-river-tuzigoot-sheep-crossing': 'The Friends of the Verde River map locates Sheep Crossing at 34.6740,-111.9412 and marks it as a difficult, long boat haul, but does not identify the water-entry edge. Keep withheld until the river landing is located and the access carry is mapped. See docs/access-remediation/2026-09-17-batch-30/review.json.',
  'upper-iowa-river-kendallville-bluffton': 'Iowa DNR confirms canoe-only access from the Bluffton Fir Stand parking area, but the stored route endpoint is a parking/access-area anchor and the DNR page does not publish the river-entry coordinate. Keep withheld until the landing edge is identified and the carry is verified. See docs/access-remediation/2026-09-17-batch-30/review.json.',
  'clearwater-river-mckays-bend-pink-house': 'BLM confirms that McKay’s Bend Recreation Site provides Clearwater River access and publishes the recreation-site coordinate, but that coordinate is not a surveyed landing. Keep withheld until the actual water entry is identified and the public approach is verified. See docs/access-remediation/2026-09-17-batch-30/review.json.',
  'rio-grande-rio-grande-village-heath-canyon': 'NPS confirms the Heath Canyon access on the U.S. side just downstream of La Linda bridge and TPWD now operates access there under a Limited Use Permit, but the stored American Whitewater coordinate is an access-area anchor rather than a verified landing. Keep withheld until the exact landing and current legal approach are georeferenced. See docs/access-remediation/2026-09-17-batch-30/review.json.',
  'wv-guyandotte-pineville-baileysville': 'Baileysville access identity is unresolved at the stored point. An older WVDNR fishing guide publishes that coordinate, but the current WVDNR GIS layer identifies the active CR 14 Bridge carry-down/pull-off about 0.8 mile east, and aerial review does not establish a legal boat carry or water entry at the stored pin. Do not substitute CR 14 without confirming it is the intended route endpoint. See docs/access-remediation/2026-09-18-batch-31-suspicious/review.json.',
  'wv-guyandotte-baileysville-rd-bailey-campground': 'Baileysville access identity is unresolved at the stored point. An older WVDNR fishing guide publishes that coordinate, but the current WVDNR GIS layer identifies the active CR 14 Bridge carry-down/pull-off about 0.8 mile east, and aerial review does not establish a legal boat carry or water entry at the stored pin. Do not substitute CR 14 without confirming it is the intended route endpoint. See docs/access-remediation/2026-09-18-batch-31-suspicious/review.json.',
  'south-fork-boise-danskin-neal': 'The Bureau of Reclamation confirms Neal Bridge as the downstream take-out, and Idaho Fish and Game identifies it with Forest Road 189, but neither reviewed source supplies a georeferenced landing. The stored RiverFacts point (43.55194,-115.73723) is about 3,900 feet west of the mapped Neal Bridge and reverse-geocodes to Blacks Creek Road. Reject the stored point and keep this expert canyon route withheld until the river-left landing before the bridge is independently located. See docs/access-remediation/2026-09-18-batch-31-suspicious/review.json.',
  'north-fork-clearwater-washington-quartz': 'Quartz Creek bridge / Forest Road 247 take-out: current reviewed sources identify the Forest Service road and a bridge vicinity but do not establish a lawful public boat take-out, parking/carry route, or water-entry coordinate. American Whitewater describes only a fair access point near the Quartz Creek confluence and other river guidance warns that Quartz Creek is not a good take-out for inflatables. Keep the route withheld until the Forest Service confirms a public landing and exact approach. See docs/access-remediation/2026-09-19-batch-115-quartz-creek-hold/review.json.',
  'boise-river-troutdale-willow': 'Willow Creek Campground take-out: the stored campground anchor is not a verified public boat landing. Reviewed Forest Service/Recreation.gov material establishes the campground and riverside setting, while current access guidance says there is no boat access at the campground. Keep the route withheld until the Forest Service confirms a lawful river carry, parking approach, and exact water entry. See docs/access-remediation/2026-09-19-batch-116-willow-creek-hold/review.json.',
